sophia: quick note after walking through the new Next starter: a couple of small but painful DX things for first-run users: env var naming, an old LlamaIndex example, and flaky eval snapshots due to streaming. repro + small fixes below.

rahul: thanks — can you paste the minimal repro for the 401?

sophia: sure. clone, cp .env.example .env, npm run dev, hit /api/complete. The example .env only documents NEXT_PUBLIC_REDWOOD_API_KEY; server code reads process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY so the secret is undefined and the API returns 401. snippet: 
```js
// pages/api/complete.js
export default async function handler(req, res) {
  const key = process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY; // undefined if user only copied NEXT_PUBLIC_ var
  const r = await fetch('https://api.redwood.ai/v1/responses', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${key}` },
    body: JSON.stringify({ input: req.body.text })
  });
  res.status(r.status).send(await r.text());
}
```

ben: yikes. users will copy the example blindly. we should make REDWOOD_API_KEY canonical in .env.example and add a big comment like "server-only secret: do not prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_".

sophia: agreed. second thing: Python LlamaIndex sample still calls generate() — JS examples show responses.create. That confuses people who jump between samples. small compat shim suggestion for python: 
```py
# samples/compat.py
from redwood import responses

def responses_create_compat(*args, **kwargs):
    if hasattr(responses, 'create'):
        return responses.create(*args, **kwargs)
    return responses.generate(*args, **kwargs)
```

rahul: add that, and note in README which SDK version introduced responses.create. also include a tiny one-line adapter in the LangChain/LlamaIndex example pointing to compat.py so forks keep working.

ben: last pain: our eval harness CI snapshots flake because some models stream tokens. CI currently runs harness in streaming mode and snapshot tests compare full strings. quick two-liner fixes: add a --capture final flag (CI uses final) and have the runner do one retry on transient network/timeouts.

sophia: also include a small withRetries util in the JS sample, but explicitly warn in README not to retry on 401s by default (that hides auth mistakes). suggested util: 
```ts
// samples/utils/withRetries.ts
export async function withRetries(fn, retries = 2) {
  let attempts = 0;
  while (true) {
    try { return await fn(); }
    catch (err) {
      if (err?.status === 401 || attempts++ >= retries) throw err;
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(null, 200 * attempts));
    }
  }
}
```

ci-bot: created issue #499 in samples: "next-starter: env var exposure, python compat, eval streaming flakes" assigned to @rahul.

doc-bot: suggested README addition: "First-run checklist: set REDWOOD_API_KEY (server-only), run evals with --capture final for CI, see samples/compat.py for SDK method mappings."

rahul: i'll bundle these into one PR: update .env.example, add withRetries util + docs caveat, add python compat shim and note, and add --capture flag to harness with CI default. will ping for review.

sophia: thanks — these are small changes but will save a lot of time for new users. :sparkles:
